    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "AIDS",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "A Pierce County judge has ruled that physicians can prescribe marijuana for medical purposes. Judge Rosanne Buckner decided that lawyer [name removed], who is undergoing treatment for bone cancer, can use marijuana to ease the pain associated with chemotherapy. Buckner ruled that the patient's interest in using marijuana as a medicine outweighs Washington's interest in outlawing prescriptions for it. Assistant Attorney General Melissa Burke-Cain plans to appeal this decision."
    }
